  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a sorted array consisting of only integers where every element appears exactly twice, except for one element which appears exactly once.\n\nOutput *the single element that appears only once*.\n\nYour solution must run in `O(log n)` time and `O(1)` space.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,1,2,3,3,4,4,8,8]\nOutput: 2\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [3,3,7,7,10,11,11]\nOutput: 10\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 105`\n* `0 <= nums[i] <= 105`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
